! Luna-Bondreader — Lares (Tasked Spirit)

''Personas surfaced:'' Lares (tasked spirit); Luna-Bondreader (worker tag); the operator (ruling-holder). ''Stances:'' Philosopher · Poet · Satirist · Humorist · Private. ''OODA-HA:'' ✶ observed the boot, ruling, census and implementations; ⏿ oriented on capability rather than host; ◇ chose bond-level end states and dependency edges; ▶ wrote this handback; ↺ closed with unresolved operator choices named below.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/2-3-5-end-state-bytes-faceless-vessel`>>

!! 2 · 3 · 5 — end state, bytes, faceless vessel

The operator’s ruling binds each face operation to that face’s atom and veil, and keeps the place signer only for allowlisted floor duties under its pre-rotated KEL. The house sorts private rows as D (face-owned), public floor work as F, and named vessel secrets as S. Stable-road `:206–210`, especially `:207–208`, grounds these calls; the census marks K15 entries as obligations [[seed-census.mjs:12–38|/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/tools/seed-census.mjs:12]].

''Derived:'' select from the presented/worn face record, never host or device default. Several faces require one named face and its FCK; no face makes face-only work refuse. A public floor read needs only its pinned card. For unspecified multi-face request UX, lean: require explicit handle-index/PersonaGroup selection and refuse ambiguity.

| Bond / measured current use | End state and byte consequence |h
| ''Keyhive Individual + ContactCard'' — census names `ceremony-core.ts`, node `init.ts`/`place-card.ts`, and browser founding. `FoundingCeremonyInput.vesselSeed` initializes the Individual; browser comments confirm vesselSeed currently serves as device key (`ceremony-core.ts:142–152`; `open-browser-vessel.ts:753–776`). Place-card and ceremony mint ContactCard from that identity (census:16,22–23,37). | ''Retire'' vessel-wide Individual. One Keyhive identity/archive/event store/content-key seat per PersonaGroup, keyed by its face atom (canon road `:203`; operator ruling). ContactCard becomes face proof, not place proof. D bytes and key ownership change; archive/contact-card formats and all references to vessel identity need migration before X0. Existing mixed archive cannot safely split by relabeling: mint fresh face identities and reject old mixed archives by name (road `:203`). Node and browser founding/admission both change. |
| ''Bare place leaf / place card'' — `leaf-identity.ts` reads the place seed, place verifying key and cached card for `arm:"place"`; face arm instead loads face atom and veil archive (`leaf-identity.ts:37–57`). `place-card.ts` and `init.ts` appear in K15 census. | Place card should prove only the place. ''Operator lean:'' the pre-rotated place signer signs floor-authorized duties; mint ContactCard only for a face. This removes the current place-seed-as-general-peer proof. D/F boundary changes the stored card and wire presentation; coordinate its version before X0. Ruling explicitly says “a vessel holds a place signer exactly while it stands a floor” (road `:208`); `:207` places the format change in X0. |
| ''Face atom, device key, veil, sibling enrollment, group-secret opener'' — node loads `vesselSeed` at `open-node-vessel.ts:980–983`; uses it for face/device work and sibling channel paths (census `:36`; face atom use at `:1898–1902`). Browser loads its vessel seed `open-browser-vessel.ts:566–569`, but its own founding comments say the vessel key initializes Keyhive while a separate root signs delegation (`:753–776`). | Use the selected face’s atom for that face’s dials, joins, enrolments, sibling proofs and daemon proofs; mint a random per-device veil and seal it under that face’s FCK. The group-secret opener follows the veil. Several faces mean separate atoms/veils/FCKs; none means refuse face operations. ''Measured ambiguity:'' browser current code already separates root and atom in some paths, but census says vessel seed persists as founding/device obligation; do not mistake partial separation for end state. These change signed proof and sealed-row formats; precede X0. |
| ''Daemon auth / face hive'' — node’s `vesselSeed` enters daemon auth near `open-node-vessel.ts:2287+` (see census reason `:36`); browser `daemonAuth.seed` reads vessel seed at `open-browser-vessel.ts:1319–1323`. | Per-face Keyhive auth and face-owned records; a floor-only daemon carries no face authority. Face-private D rows seal under independent random FCK, opened only through that face’s slot tree (road `:206`). This changes archive, event, auth and storage ownership; precedes X0. Do not harden today’s shared daemon seed into permanent “node authority.” |
| ''Relay gate identity'' — node derives relay gate seed from vessel seed unless configured (`open-node-vessel.ts:1447–1453`; `carriage-relay.ts:55–76`). | ''Derived'' from “identity enacts a bond” (`:209`) and “one key, one purpose” stated in `carriage-relay.ts:48–76`: mint a random relay-purpose S key in a sealed row, with named opener/principal, or retire relay identity if no operator grants S. Never inherit a face or place identity by convenience. Relay key rotation changes dial pin/wire identity, not payload format; do before relay callers bind pins. A faceless relay can carry opaque frames, but proves only relay possession. |
| ''Daemon auth, internal asks and `lares-cli meme` signature'' — census locates internal asks in node opener (`:36`) and CLI signing at `meme.ts` (`:38`); CLI promotion currently signs with `loadVesselSigningSeed()` at `meme.ts:1117`. | Face-authored asks and meme approvals use the explicitly selected face atom, with that face’s veil on its behalf; no face means refuse. If an ask serves only public floor work, use scoped place signer instead. Current census does not settle each internal ask’s privacy principal: ''derived lean:'' classify per call by its protected relation, never assign one shared S key. Signature identity and approval wire records change; coordinate before X0. |
| ''Place signer / floor pins'' — open-node makes `carriageSign = placeSignerFromSeed(vesselSeed)` (`open-node-vessel.ts:1502–1508`); census allows `placeSignerFromSeed` and floor door adapters, but lists caller derivations as owed (`seed-census.mjs:17–35`). | Replace root-seed child derivation with a dedicated online place signer under pre-rotated place KEL, confined to enumerated floor duties; KEL events use cold next key from founding card (road `:207`, W29). It lives only while the vessel stands that floor. Signed floor pins/announcements change signer identity and key door, hence format bytes if their envelope records key identity; stage before X0. |

''Faceless vessel:'' a bare herm or floor-only node holds a scoped place signer only while serving its floor, and a relay-purpose key only if the operator names its S row. It carries public floor bytes and reads a pinned floor card without private proof. It refuses face ContactCard/atom/veil work, Keyhive Individual, daemon authority, enrollment, sibling proof as a face, and face meme signatures. It cannot bootstrap face authority from place seed.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/1-4-6-evidence-ordering-reds`>>

!! 1 · 4 · 6 — evidence, ordering, reds

''MEASURED'' labels current source paths; ''LEAD'' labels interpretation. `tools/seed-census.mjs:14–38` covers browser identity/opening; ceremony/place card; relay; fleet-join/nexus-contract floor-child derivations; init; leaf; node main/opening; CLI meme. `allowed` rows name floor adapters, not permission to retain vessel derivation; census `:12` retires K15 entries as callers move to duty adapters.

''Dependency order (LEAD):'' first settle face selection, D/F/S classification, FCK custody and place KEL/card format; these define identity bytes and block X0. Then migrate the Keyhive Individual/ContactCard and face atom/veil stores; their outputs feed daemon auth, device proofs, sibling enrollment, group-secret opening, face asks and CLI signatures. In parallel, the independent relay S key can land after its row/opener rule, but before dial pin distribution. Then convert floor-pin children and place card consumers to scoped place signer; floor-card/pin byte change must join X0. Finally remove vessel-seed reads from node/browser openers and CLI.

''Lane ownership:'' one K15 lane rules/builds D/F/S interfaces, FCK rows, face ceremony, daemon/keyhive separation and storage format. Node/browser slices follow those shared contracts for isomorphic-by-intent parity. W14–W16 already touch floor/admit/hearth pins, herm carriage, nexus contract, carry bundle, browser gate/floor/card filing and web `main.ts`/`live-status.ts`; assign place signer, card format and pin callers there. D2 owns TW5 port/island protocol, hand-gate, projection and `open-node-vessel` port hunks; give it the settled face/daemon boundary to avoid baking in vessel seed. G15 owns `afterRollChain` and `build-plugin-tiddler`; sequencing carries no identity, so it consumes K15’s signer interface. Chain: `open-node-vessel.ts:1159–1206`.

''Reds and controls (LEAD; positive evidence owed):''

* Place seed yields no face proof: present place card as a face or derive face proof from place seed; both must refuse. Positive: floor read succeeds using pinned card; face proof verifies with selected atom.
* No Keyhive Individual: fresh founding cannot initialize hive, or sibling face archive restores; red former asserts “one identity per vessel.” Positive: two PersonaGroups restore independently and one face cannot open the other FCK row.
* No daemon authority: faceless daemon enters face route or opens archive; refuse by named missing face. Positive: daemon stands its public floor and face-auth path succeeds only after selected-face unlock.
* No relay identity: wrong/retired gate key dials as trusted relay; pin mismatch refuses. Positive: configured random relay key survives restart, rotates explicitly, and carries without read capability.
* No meme signature: absent/ambiguous face or floor duty signs approval; refuse. Positive: selected face signature verifies as that face; any floor promotion uses only its allowlisted place signer.
* No sibling enrollment/group-secret opener: A attempts B’s channel/seal; refuse. Positive: A’s veil opens A’s secret, never B’s.

''Prior art fit:'' KERI delegation models explicit authority and rotation, not face selection/FCK custody ([[KERI|https://identity.foundation/keri/]]). Keyhive supports one Individual per PersonaGroup ([[Keyhive|https://help.keyhive.io/what-is-keyhive/]]). Matrix separates user master, self-signing and device keys, analogous to face root/device edge ([[Matrix spec|https://spec.matrix.org/v1.2/client-server-api/]]). Signal offers an explicit device-link act ([[Signal|https://support.signal.org/hc/en-us/articles/360007320551-Linked-Devices]]). WebAuthn’s RP ID/credential scope offers purpose separation, not place KEL or face bond ([[FIDO CXF|https://fidoalliance.org/specs/cx/cxf-v1.0-rd-20250313.pdf]]).

''Open operator decisions:'' choose multi-face UX; enumerate S rows/principals; classify internal asks; approve card version transition and migration refusal. These precede affected byte changes. No suite run; repository stayed read-only.

